-## [Unreleased]
+## [0.4.0] - 2026-10-22
+
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool `input` against the declared `inputSchema` using `ajv`. A rejection returns a `ToolResponse` with a descriptive error message instead of throwing, allowing the model to correct the call in the next round.
+- Rejection messages and logs name failing property paths and constraints but never echo property values, preventing data leakage.
+- Function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` now has its returned `inputSchema` compiled and cached per-call.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Breaking:** `ToolRegistry.register` now pre-compiles a static tool's `inputSchema` and throws naming the tool if the schema is invalid JSON Schema.
+- Tool executors now only receive input that has already passed the declared schema.
 
